Spell a named construction's head as authored, as the positional path does

Dev accepted the one recommendation restated from Codex's October 26 handoff: spell the
named-construction head as authored or resolved, the same as the positional path, with one
cross-package compile-and-run test checking scoped and unscoped generation. The reading was
verified first by a direct probe: DracoGenerator.constructionInitializer spelled the SLOT
TYPE's last segment, so a Consumer variant constructing domains.terrestrial.Location with
named arguments generated bare `Location(_latitude = …)` in domains.world and scalac refused
it ("not found: value Location"). The positional path renders the head verbatim, which is why
the accepted Consumer compiles.

The repair is one line in constructionInitializer: the head is `expression(operands.head)`,
the applied head as the author or the scope in effect spelled it, never the slot type's last
segment. The factory check and the `_name` parameter mapping are unchanged. Unscoped, a
cross-package construction keeps its qualification; scoped, the engine shortens it to the bare
name and adds the selective import, as it does every resolvable name. Consumer's accepted
positional call is untouched. No general constructor redesign and no other example repair.

Corpus impact, measured before building: only three definitions carry a named argument, all
examples. aerial/Input authors its own package's Position bare, so it renders bare before and
after; terrestrial/Output is not intercepted, LocationReport having no factory; world/Observable's
construction sits in a dyn body, which renders through expression with no `_` mapping. Old and
new engine generate byte-identical Scala for Input, Output, Observable and Consumer, so no
committed file regenerates. Two adjacent observations were surfaced, not recommended: the
method keys its factory lookup on the slot type rather than the head, and a dyn-body result
never maps named parameters to the factory's `_` convention (Observable authors `_geocentric`).

NamedConstructionTest (3) is new, the 72nd suite: a probe authored in domains.world constructs
domains.terrestrial.Location with named arguments inside a global dyn; the generated file
imports only `draco._` and `domains._`, so no import masks the head's spelling. Unscoped, the
qualified head is asserted; scoped through the example scope, the bare head plus its selective
import; both generations are compiled with the runtime compiler and run, and the constructed
Location carries the authored values. The third test pins an own-package head authored bare
staying bare, as Input spells Position.

